                                "sense_id": "a0840f1e-b175-37d0-935e-60e3fbf77ec6",
                                "text": "It attenuateth[…]crude and colde humours, and flatuosities abounding in flegmatike and melancholicke persons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e87a11f-ebe8-465c-b87a-8bb716075617",
                                "sense_id": "a0840f1e-b175-37d0-935e-60e3fbf77ec6",
                                "text": "The fourth cause is flatuosity : for wind stirred moveth to expel : and we find that ( in effect ) all purgers have in them a raw spirit or wind ; which is the principal cause of tortion in the stomach and belly"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6363064c-9690-4b80-b5e4-092208e8d3d3",
                                "sense_id": "a0840f1e-b175-37d0-935e-60e3fbf77ec6",
                                "text": "Remove that flatuosity, which is the cause of thy Disease."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
